<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet xml:id="diaMuertos-ws-fullFiesta">
  <title>The Full Fiesta</title>

  <exercise>
    <!-- <title>Building all the músicos</title> -->
    <!-- <introduction> -->
      <p>At the full fiesta:
        <ul>
          <li><p>All músicos are different</p></li>
          <li><p>All possible músicos that you can think of are in there!</p></li>
        </ul>
      </p>
      <p>Remember the four aspects and their choices:</p>

                    <tabular>
        <row bottom="medium" header="yes"><cell>Aspect</cell><cell>Choices</cell><cell>Codes</cell></row>
        <row><cell>Face</cell><cell>Fox, Gato, Human</cell><cell>F, G, H</cell></row>
        <row><cell>Body</cell><cell>Suit, Bones, Dress</cell><cell>Su, Bo, Dr</cell></row>
        <row><cell># of Jaranas</cell><cell>2, 1, 0</cell><cell>2, 1, 0</cell></row>
        <row><cell>Gift</cell><cell>bread, chocolate, dalia</cell><cell>br, ch, da</cell></row>
      </tabular>
    <!-- </introduction> -->
    
    <p>
    <ol>
      <li workspace="6cm">
        <p>We want to build <alert>all</alert> the músicos in the fiesta. What is a good strategy we can use to make sure that (i) we do not forget anyone, and (ii) we do not repeat anyone? Illustrate the process with 1 picture (or more!).</p>
      </li>
      <li workspace="2cm">
        <p>
        Complete the sentence: <q>I made sure that I built all the músicos and without repeating any of them because . . . </q>
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    </p>
  </exercise>

  <exercise workspace="8cm">
    <!-- <title>How many músicos are at the fiesta?</title> -->
    <statement>
      <p>All the músicos came to the fiesta. How many of them are there?</p>
      <ol>
        <li><p>Make your own prediction.</p></li>
        <li><p>Find an effective way of counting them.</p></li>
        <li><p>Explain your method to everyone!</p></li>
        <li><p>
            <line>Bonus: can you generalize?</line> 
            <line>(What if there are more aspects? Or more choices in one aspect?)</line>
          </p></li>
      </ol>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

</worksheet>
